ning (H1-H2):** payload-depth re-scan superseding the served-text backfill\n  (monotonic toward non-servable); promote the evidence-rigor loop out of shadow with a real metered\n  per-iteration score_fn + an engine-diff CLI + a tightened promotion gate (defaults to legacy).\n- **llm.py upgrades (L1-L6):** a cost-telemetry substrate first (so discount features are metered\n  correctly), then prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive-`effort` thinking, model retargeting,\n  and the Message Batches API.\n\n## Success criteria\n- Every servable artifact carries a payload-depth `security_status`; benign-description/malicious-payload is caught; the re-stamp is monotonic toward non-servable.\n- The evidence loop has a real metered per-iteration score_fn + a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py` enforcing the promotion gate; the live flip stays default-off.\n- `llm.py` supports prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive `effort`, current model tiers, and an opt-in batch path â€” all with correct CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml metering (regression-tested).\n- Locked-preserved intact: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n\n## Hard constraints\n- Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass; the gate stays single-owner (`roles/security/gate.py`).\n- The metered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and OUT of the build waves â€” waves build machinery + run shadow only.\n- Every LLM call meters through CostRecorder against a matching pricing.yaml key; the Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback, tenacity retry, and `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI` kill-switch are preserved.\n- test-command: `python -m pytest`. No test weakening; the test count may only rise.\n\n## Provenance\nSource plans (committed): `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` (H1-H2) and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`\n(L1-L6), each code-grounded by a Plan sub-agent. Combined + ordered he