{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0123uByciCGRzNWXmyjQy3M7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# foreman-handoff-phase2 â€” Grounded Summary\n\n**Source:** `docs/foreman-handoff-phase2/` (DESCRIPTION.md + IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md, Foreman-ready combined). Build half of the researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict in `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md`.\n\n## Framing / North Star\n- The plan closes two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's **live verdict path** AND adopts cheap modern Anthropic API capabilities Aurora is missing â€” explicitly **evolving `llm.py` + the security path, not rebuilding the architecture**.\n- Rationale carried from the AuroraTwo research: fan-out is \"theater at TOP_K=2-3\"; the value sits in the LLM layer + security/evidence path, which already exist and only need hardening/upgrading.\n- **Locked-preserved (must stay intact):** KB schema + library, single-owner security gate (`roles/security/gate.py`), deterministic cost telemetry (CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml), Helping Hand + publisher.\n- **Hard constraints:** no seam may produce an unearned pass on the live path; every LLM call meters through CostRecorder against a matching pricing.yaml key; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback, tenacity retry, and `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI` kill-switch preserved; test-command `python -m pytest`; **no test weakening â€” count may only rise**.\n- **Out of scope (separately authorized):** the metered evidence-shadow batch (**SA-1**) and the live promotion flip (**SA-2**). Waves build machinery + run shadow only.\n\n## Structure\n- **8 waves, run in series** (threads overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge). Two threads:\n  - **Security hardening** = Waves 1â€“2 (H1â€“H2)\n  - **`llm.py` upgrades** = Waves 3â€“8 (L1â€“L6), cost-telemetry substrate first so discount features meter correctly.\n- Per-thread rationale lives in source plans `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` (H1â€“H2) and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md` (L1â€“L6), each code-grounded by a Plan sub-agent.\n\n## Wave-by-wave claims\n- **Wave 1 â€” H1 Payload-depth scan:** Supersede the W2 served-text backfill (artifacts stamped `clean-with-notes` from name+short_description) by re-fetching each artifact's real payload from `canonical_url` and re-stamping `security_status`. Deterministic detectors only â€” **no LLM cost** (judge/sandbox default-off). Payloads aren't retained on disk, so it re-fetches via existing `bin/run_security_shadow.py::_run_pipeline` machinery (7-day tarball cache). New `bin/scan_payload_depth.py`; **monotonic toward non-servable** (worst-wins, clean rows untouched); failed/stale fetch â†’ `extraction-incomplete`, fail-closed. Scannable set â‰ˆ **775 artifacts**.\n- **Wave 2 â€” H2 Evidence-loop promotion machinery:** Add a real metered per-iteration `score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py` (re-runs critic_a/b/câ†’reconciler over the deepened corpus, every call metered), a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py`, and a metered shadow batch to populate `validations_shadow` (0 rows today). Promotion gate enforces **agreementâ‰¥0.95, min_samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—**. Live switch `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop` **defaults to legacy**; flip is SA-1/SA-2, not done here.\n- **Wave 3 â€” L1 Cost-telemetry substrate:** Migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` adds nullable `cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `batch_mode`. pricing.yaml gets cache sub-rates (read â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input, write â‰ˆ1.25Ã— input) + top-level `batch_discount: 0.5`. `CostRecorder.record` extended; **legacy 4-arg call sites byte-for-byte identical**. Built before any feature emits these tokens (safety-first).\n- **Wave 4 â€” L2 Prompt caching:** `cache_control:{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}` on stable system+rubric prefixes for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; reads `cache_read_input_tokens`/`cache_creation_input_tokens` into CostRecorder; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the same cache_control.\n- **Wave 5 â€” L3 Structured outputs:** Replace `json.loads(strip_fences(...))` with schema-guaranteed JSON on critic/reconciler/security-judge paths (one shared verdict schema in `roles/contracts.py`); off-schema judge response still **fails closed to `abstain`**; Gemini langextract path stays as-is.\n- **Wave 6 â€” L4 Adaptive thinking via `effort`:** Adopt `effort`; **never send `budget_tokens`** (deprecated 4.6+, returns 400 on Opus 4.8) with a loud guard; fold API-reported thinking tokens into metered output (root cause of the prior **$118 incident**).\n- **Wave 7 â€” L5 Model retargeting:** Retarget defaults to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5); add `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; **1.35 for 4.7+**) applied **only to pre-call estimates, never to post-call metering** (real `resp.usage` stays ground-truth).\n- **Wave 8 â€” L6 Message Batches API:** Opt-in async batch path for nightly sweeps (~50% discount) behind `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (**default off**); per-item failure degrades to synchronous via `_note_degrade` (sweep never aborts); missing security-judge batch result â†’ `abstain`, fail-closed; flag-off path byte-for-byte the current pipeline.\n\n## Cross-cutting acceptance pattern\n- Every wave's \"done-when\" ends with **`pytest` green, no test weakening**, and the **single-owner security gate test still passing**.\n- Recurring SUBTLE/regression invariants: legacy cost path unchanged, batch = exactly 0.5Ã—, cache-read â‰ˆ0.1Ã—, no `budget_tokens` ever assembled, tokenizer factor on estimates only, and no swap/feature can beat legacy leniency without tripping an unearned-pass FAIL.\n\nWant me to also capture this as an Aurora project memory, or is the summary the deliverable?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8461,"cache_read_input_tokens":34002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8461},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inferenc